      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To suggest that we can simply turn a blind eye to suffering overseas is a moral failure of the highest order. Our commitment to human dignity demands that we act when people are starving, oppressed, or facing preventable disasters. Foreign aid isn't charity; it is a fundamental investment in global stability and the shared humanity we claim to uphold. We have a moral obligation to alleviate suffering, and that obligation transcends national borders.",
      "source": "target",
