      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The argument that aid is inherently wasted due to corruption is a cynical excuse for inaction, not a factual critique of the entire endeavor. Smart, targeted aid programs bypass corrupt structures by empowering local communities directly, fostering self-sufficiency from the ground up. Furthermore, investing in global health and education yields massive returns by stabilizing regions, which ultimately benefits the entire international economy. We must support innovative, transparent models that prove the efficacy of global partnership.",
      "source": "target",
